omes mandatory. This\n  package carries that glossary as its schemas and renders each report as\n  incident-report.md, every field under its number.\n\n  Supply three inputs in a data directory:\n\n  - stage, field 1.1, the type of submission: \"initial notification\",\n    \"intermediate report\" or \"final report\";\n  - entity, section 1 of the template: who submits the report, for which\n    financial entity, and whom to contact;\n  - incident, sections 2, 3 and 4: the incident itself.\n\n  Read [what the stage decides](inputs/incident.md) before filling the\n  incident in. The stage decides which fields are mandatory. Section 2's\n  are mandatory at every stage, section 3's from the intermediate report\n  on, and section 4's in the final report. A field the stage does not yet\n  require may be given early, and is then checked like any other.\n\n  Each report updates the one before it. Keep one data directory per\n  incident, and for each new report change stage, add the fields the stage\n  adds and correct what has changed:\n\n      metais validate dora-incident-report --data incident\n      metais render dora-incident-report --data incident --out report\n\n  validate reports every mandatory field the stage still lacks, and every\n  value that does not fit its field's type, all at once. Each schema's\n  properties carry the glossary's field number as x-field and its type as\n  x-field-type; metais schema dora-incident-report incident shows them.\n\n  The package renders the content of a report. It does not file it: send\n  it to your competent authority in the form and through the channel that\n  authority prescribes. The package's [references](references/sources.md)\n  name the legal texts it is written from and their reuse terms.\ninputs:\n  - name: stage\n    title: \"1.1 Type of submission\"\n    description: \"Which of the three reports on the incident this is: the initial notification, the intermediate report or the final report.\"\n    schema: inputs/stage.schema.json\n    forms:\n      - json\n      - yaml\n  - name: entity\n    title: \"The financial entity\"\n    description: \"Section 1 of the template: the entity submitting the report, the financial entity affected, and whom to contact.\"\n    schema: inputs/entity.schema.json\n    forms:\n      - json\n      - yaml\n  - name: incident\n    title: \"The incident\"\n    description: \"Sections 2, 3 and 4 of the template: the incident, as this stage's report states it.\"\n    schema: inputs/incident.schema.json\n    meaning: inputs/incident.md\n    forms:\n      - json\n      - yaml\ninput_constraints: inputs/constraints.schema.json\noutputs:\n  - id: report\n    template: incident-report.md.liquid","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"edbb6e52-13de-4242-9ee7-038b810dad24","uuid":"f0b610bf-e631-4001-b8c4-cfa7843b6fb1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:10:09.097Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/bin/bash: /etc/bash.bashrc: Permission denied\nREADME.md 540\n.compiled/digests.json 2743\n.compiled/manifest.json 3342\n.compiled/references.json 118\n.compiled/schema.json 42783\nexamples/final/example.yaml 163\nexamples/final/expected/incident-report.md 6399\nexamples/final/inputs/entity.json 617\nexamples/final/inputs/incident.json 3986\nexamples/final/inputs/stage.json 15\nexamples/initial/example.yaml 158\nexamples/initial/expected/incident-report.md 2073\nexamples/initial/inputs/entity.json 617\nexamples/initial/inputs/incident.json 831\nexamples/initial/inputs/stage.json 23\nexamples/intermediate/example.yaml 188\nexamples/intermediate/expected/incident-report.md 4950\nexamples/intermediate/inputs/entity.json 617\nexamples/intermediate/inputs/incident.json 2929\nexamples/intermediate/inputs/stage.json 22\ninputs/constraints.schema.json 13221\ninputs/entity.schema.json 8769\ninputs/incident.md 3442\ninputs/incident.schema.json 35847\ninputs/stage.schema.json 382\nmetais.yaml 3404\nreferences/sources.md 4964\ntemplates/incident-report.md.liquid 14131\nmetais: \"1.0\"\nname: \"dora-incident-report\"\nversion: \"1.0.0\"\ntitle: \"DORA major ICT-related incident report\"\ndescription: \"Renders a financial entity's report on a major ICT-related incident under Regulation (EU) 2022/2554 (DORA), at each of its three stages, from the fields of the template of Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/302.\"\nlicense: \"Apache-2.0\"\nguide: |-\n  A financial entity that classifies an ICT-related incident as major\n  reports it to its competent authority three times, on one template: an\n  initial notification, an intermediate report and a final report.\n  Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/302 lays down the template in its\n  Annex I and its data glossary in its Annex II, which numbers every field,\n  gives its type, and says at which stage it becomes mandatory. This\n  package carries that glossary as its schemas and renders each report as\n  incident-report.md, every field under its number.\n\n  Supply three inputs in a data directory:\n\n  - stage, field 1.1, the type of submission: \"initial notification\",\n    \"intermediate report\" or \"final report\";\n  - entity, section 1 of the template: who submits the report, for which\n    financial entity, and whom to contact;\n  - incident, sections 2, 3 and 4: the incident itself.\n\n  Read [what the stage decides](inputs/incident.md) before filling the\n  incident in. The stage decides which fields are mandatory. Section 2's\n  are mandatory at every stage, section 3's from the intermediate report\n  on, and section 4's in the final report. A field the stage does not yet\n  require may be given early, and is then checked like any other.\n\n  Each report updates the one before it. Keep one data directory per\n  incident, and for each new report change stage, add the fields the stage\n  adds and correct what has changed:\n\n      metais validate dora-incident-report --data incident\n      metais render dora-incident-report --data incident --out report\n\n  validate reports every mandatory field the stage still lacks, and every\n  value that does not fit its field's type, all at once. Each schema's\n  properties carry the glossary's field number as x-field and its type as\n  x-field-type; metais schema dora-incident-report incident shows them.\n\n  The package renders the content of a report. It does not file it: send\n  it to your competent authority in the form and through the channel that\n  authority prescribes. The package's [references](references/sources.md)\n  name the legal texts it is written from and their reuse terms.\ninputs:\n  - name: stage\n    title: \"1.1 Type of submission\"\n    description: \"Which of the three reports on the incident this is: the initial notification, the intermediate report or the final report.\"\n    schema: inputs/stage.schema.json\n    forms:\n      - json\n      - yaml\n  - name: entity\n    title: \"The financial entity\"\n    description: \"Section 1 of the template: the entity submitting the report, the financial entity affected, and whom to contact.\"\n    schema: inputs/entity.schema.json\n    forms:\n      - json\n      - yaml\n  - name: incident\n    title: \"The incident\"\n    description: \"Sections 2, 3 and 4 of the template: the incident, as this stage's report states it.\"\n    schema: inputs/incident.schema.json\n    meaning: inputs/incident.md\n    forms:\n      - json\n      - yaml\ninput_constraints: inputs/constraints.schema.json\noutputs:\n  - id: report\n    template: incident-report.md.liquid","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LnNaikaVWWiFZBefp1uvft","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
