puts pointer, such as /vendor/name=Acme; the text is\n      coerced to the type the schema declares there. Applied after --data and\n      --inputs-json, in command-line order with --set-json. May be given more\n      than once.\n  --set-json <pointer>=<json>\n      Set one value at an inputs pointer as JSON text, the way to set null, an\n      array or an object. Applied in command-line order with --set. May be given\n      more than once.\n  --inputs-json <json>\n      A JSON object whose members are inputs, each replacing that input's whole\n      value; - reads it from standard input, once. Applied after --data, in\n      command-line order. May be given more than once.\n  --resolved\n      Add the inputs as templates would see them: parsed and coerced, with\n      defaults applied, absent members absent.\n  --limit <name>=<value>\n      Lower one resource limit for this run, to a whole number no higher than\n      its default (a size may end in KiB, MiB or GiB). metais limits lists them.\n      May be given more than once.\n  --fail-on <severity>\n      With warning, a warning fails the command with exit status 1 as an error\n      does; no finding's severity changes. Values: error, warning. Default:\n      error.\n  --json\n      Print the result as one JSON document on standard output.\n  --color <when>\n      Colour human output: auto colours a stream that is a terminal when\n      NO_COLOR is unset or empty; always and never override NO_COLOR. Values:\n      auto, always, never. Default: auto.\n  -h, --help\n      Print help to standard output and exit 0; nothing else runs.\n\nPrints:\n  Every finding, then the summary line; with --resolved, the inputs as indented\n  JSON. With --json, one metais.validate/1 document.\n\nRefusals:\n  limit.invalid\n      A --limit names no limit, gives a malformed value, or tries to raise one.\n      Next: metais limits\n  limit.package\n      The package breaches one of its limits.\n      Next: metais limits\n  usage.bad_value\n      A flag's value is missing, or is not one the flag accepts, or a flag that\n      takes no value is given one.\n      Next: metais validate --help\n  usage.conflicting_flags\n      --inputs-json - is given twice, and standard input is read once.\n      Next: metais help inputs\n  usage.data_dir_unreadable\n      The data directory given to --data does not exist, is not a directory, or\n      cannot be read.\n      Next: metais help inputs\n  usage.missing_operand\n      The package operand is not given.\n      Next: metais validate --help\n  usage.package_from_stdin\n      The package operand is -, standard input.\n      Next: metais validate --help\n  usage.repeated_flag\n      A flag that may be given once is given again.\n      Next: metais validate --help\n  usage.unexpected_operand\n      An operand the command does not take.\n      Next: metais validate --help\n  usage.unknown_flag\n      An argument that is not a flag the command accepts, an abbreviated flag,\n      or one-letter aliases written together.\n      Next: metais validate --help\n\n  Each line below is a family of codes: how many there are, the cause they share\n  and their next step. 'metais help refusals validate' lists every code, and\n  help --json gives each code's own cause.\n\n  manifest.* (44)  The manifest breaks one of its rules.\n                   Next: metais inspect <package>\n  package.* (47)   The package is refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n  schema.* (10)    An input schema is refused. Next: metais inspect <package>\n  template.* (9)   An output's path, when or for_each does not parse.\n                   Next: metais inspect <package>\n\nExamples:\n  metais validate report-1.0.0.metais --data data\n      Validates the inputs in the directory data.\n  metais validate report-1.0.0.metais --data data --set /vendor/name=Acme\n      Validates them with one value replaced.\n  metais validate report-1.0.0.metais --inputs-json - --json\n      Validates the inputs object read from standard input, and prints one\n      metais.validate/1 document.\n  metais validate report-1.0.0.metais --data data --resolved\n      Validates them and prints the inputs as templates would see them.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GA3fe1VdDLz7cn2YNUBfYK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
